id: SceneVariants
name: ᝯㄝₓ Scene Variants
metadata:
  description: "A scene is often in your library twice: the whole thing, and a cut out of it. Stash has no way to say the two are the same work, so this plugin works it out and gives the scene page a tab that shows you.\n\nOpen any scene and there is a Variants tab beside Details, File Info and Edit. It lists every other scene sharing this one's stash-id, with the cover image and the preview loop it plays on hover, its resolution and running time, longest first - and where there is nothing to list it says why. The tab itself writes nothing: it is two read queries and a list of links. Hover a row and it tells you how that variant differs from the scene you are on: the tags it has that this one does not, the tags it is missing, and the names of the attributes that disagree - which fields differ, not what either of them says.\n\nName your full-length and partial-length tags below and each row says which it is, with the full-length ones sorted to the top - that is the question the tab exists to answer, and the tags are the cheap half of it. A name matches any of the tag's aliases too, and a scene tagged with anything under that tag in your hierarchy counts as tagged with it, so naming the general tag covers every specific one beneath it. Rows read Full-length and Partial-length rather than echoing your tag names back; the tag that decided a row is on its hover text. Leave both names empty and the tab still lists the variants, just without saying which is which.\n\nA stash-id, or the variant stash-id custom field this plugin's migration task writes, is the evidence used - a partial-length cut should not carry a real stash-id, because that id names the whole work, so the task moves it into a field of its own and the tab matches on both. A scene that never got one, or whose variants never got one, gets a tab that says so; matching on titles and on shared performers is not built yet, so about two scenes in three have nothing to list today. A scene carrying both tags at once is shown in red, because the two are meant to be exclusive.\n\nRequires Stash 0.28.0 or newer: the tab is added through the scene page's own plugin extension points, so there is no version of it that works without them."
